  "grammar": {
    "title": "Adverbs in -ment + instructions",
    "intro": "To say how you do something (gently, quickly…), take the feminine adjective and add -ment, like -ly in English. Recipes use the imperative (vous or tu form) for instructions.",
    "table": [
      [
        "Adjective (m / f)",
        "Adverb",
        "Rule"
      ],
      [
        "doux / douce",
        "doucement",
        "feminine + -ment"
      ],
      [
        "rapide",
        "rapidement",
        "ends in -e: just add -ment"
      ],
      [
        "vrai",
        "vraiment",
        "ends in a vowel: masculine + -ment"
      ],
      [
        "lent / lente",
        "lentement",
        "feminine + -ment"
      ],
      [
        "bon / bien",
        "bien",
        "irregular"
      ],
      [
        "mauvais / mal",
        "mal",
        "irregular"
      ]
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "fr": "Coupe les oignons finement.",
        "en": "Chop the onions finely."
      },
      {
        "fr": "Faites cuire doucement pendant dix minutes.",
        "en": "Cook gently for ten minutes."
      },
      {
        "fr": "Elle cuisine vraiment bien.",
        "en": "She cooks really well."
      }
    ],
    "trap": "Adjectives in -ant / -ent become -amment / -emment, both pronounced « amment »: évident → évidemment, couramment. The adverb goes after the verb: « il parle lentement ». Imperative with pronouns: « fais-les cuire », « mélange-le »."
  },
  "sounds": {
